    "Description": "This is a kernel live patch module which can be loaded by the kpatch command line utility to modify the code of a running kernel.  This patch module is targeted for kernel-5.14.0-687.10.1.el9_8.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: smb: client: validate dacloffset before building DACL pointers (CVE-2026-46195)\n\n* kernel: ipc: limit next_id allocation to the valid ID range (CVE-2026-52923)\n\n* kernel: udp: fix potential use-after-free in tunnel segmentation (CVE-2026-74705)\n\n* kernel: net: tun: bound receive headroom (CVE-2026-81000)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
